# Python-generated files
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info

# coverage.py's data file (`just coverage`). It is a required intermediate —
# `coverage run` writes it and `coverage report` reads it — not an incidental
# artifact, so it is always there after the recipe runs and a `git add -A`
# would otherwise take it.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Virtual environments
.venv
.uv/

# Data warehouse & downloaded sources (regenerated by the pipeline)
data/*.duckdb
data/*.duckdb.wal
data/raw/
# The CBAM annex workbook, if `scripts/build_cbam_seeds.py` was run without
# `--xlsx`. The seeds it produces are checked in; the 860 kB source is not.
data/*.xlsx
# Publishable artifact built by `just export-data`; it lives in GitHub releases
data/export/
# Leftovers from the hive Parquet archive, which DuckLake replaced. **Keep this
# entry.** The layer is gone but the directory is not: any clone that ran
# `just lake` still has 793 files and 60 MB of it on disk, and dropping the
# line stages every one of them on the next `git add -A` — measured, on the
# commit that removed the layer.
data/lake/
# Downloads kept between runs so a partitioned load doesn't re-fetch a 45 MB zip
# per partition. Byte-identical to what the URL still serves — safe to delete.
data/cache/
# The course sandbox (`just course-sandbox`): a fixture warehouse the exercises
# in docs/course/ break on purpose. Rebuilt in ~40s; safe to delete.
data/course/
*.csv
!dbt/seeds/*.csv
# Unit-test fixtures. Same exception as the seeds and for the same reason: the
# blanket rule above is aimed at downloaded data, and these are source. Without
# this line `dbt test` passes locally against files git never took, and CI fails
# on a fixture that is not there.
!dbt/tests/fixtures/*.csv

# dbt
dbt/target/
dbt/dbt_packages/
dbt/logs/
dbt/.user.yml
# dbt takes this lock around package state and does not always remove it — an
# empty file that `git status` then reports as untracked, which is one stray
# `git add -A` away from being committed.
dbt/package-lock.concurrent-update-lock

# dlt
.dlt/secrets.toml
**/.dlt/pipelines/

# Dagster instance: run/event storage, compute logs (DAGSTER_HOME).
# The checked-in dagster.yaml is config; everything beside it is state.
.dagster/*
!.dagster/dagster.yaml
.tmp_dagster_home_*/

# Evidence
reports/.evidence/
reports/build/
node_modules/

# Claude Code session transcripts and scratch notes. They're kept locally as a
# working record but not committed — a `git add -A` would otherwise sweep in
# whatever the last session left here. The three files tracked before this rule
# landed stay tracked; `git add -f` for anything new that's worth keeping.
docs/sessions/

# The DuckLake landing zone: where dlt writes `raw`. Filled by `just ingest`,
# not by `just lakehouse` (which only reports on it). **This is the one
# gitignored path that holds state no rebuild reproduces** — the snapshot
# lineage, and the capital-city weather archive, which costs days of
# Open-Meteo's daily allowance to refetch. `just clean` deliberately skips it.
data/lakehouse/
